answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437580} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd678d7-15ac-548b-b810-649d7913e7db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cd678d7-15ac-548b-b810-649d7913e7db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437581} :answer-field/id #uuid "de2afb91-baf3-53b2-8e4a-7316ea92bfe0" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "635d0331-704b-5958-9f79-2f8d94fa4111" :question/math-academy-id "q-119797" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(2-x)(y+1)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(2-x)(y+1).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=2$ or $y=-1.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/ca/caa61190f1a5565c58838556529715c08f9f00402c6f4b3ccb99a914e748f198.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/01/01e91ecf01cfc64ed87e29081a6b9f8a3fc5afade1b25be08039b8778d981cf7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $x>2$ and $y<-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative” is true. If $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive”; “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative”; “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive”."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e1be2fa-de0d-5f22-b440-911091c56105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437582} {:answer/id #uuid "75d08e9a-c55b-5a67-abb2-4e27159b9b63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e1be2fa-de0d-5f22-b440-911091c56105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437582} :answer-field/id #uuid "8390e0db-2166-50f2-a123-b7b9177c8341" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y>2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id 