8fa703a63eee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14479ff4-2e02-5757-a626-8fa703a63eee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667893} :answer-field/id #uuid "52c518f8-757a-57a1-b9fe-e5ced44e0f67" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dff46479-0340-5239-b8ff-db620f2c9a7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-119800" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(1-x)(y-2)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(1-x)(y-2).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=1$ or $y=2.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/47/47784a3201e93648e495827b12078073cc9f1a03cd3c11904a875bad10a3bde2.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/73/73631c178777b4489e35fa87d08474ccf2b8b484b9bf5fe7272b1ce25d45f1b0.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y>2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $x<1$ and $y>2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $x>1$ and $y<2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive” is false. If $x<1$ and $y<2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253607 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9e11f01-32e2-5138-b450-b28abfcfe393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437588} {:answer/id #uuid "eba29a8a-cdc7-5437-a377-49e424a33c92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9e11f01-32e2-5138-b450-b28abfcfe393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437588} :answer-field/id #uuid "6731a097-fbbb-5d0d-924d-44214b41bafb" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67be040e-e5a2-539e-bae4-03679cb8d0dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437590} {:answer/id #uuid "989c32ec-026e-53bf-8bf8-04e72bb618bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "989c32ec-026e-53bf-8bf8-04e72bb618bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437591} :answer-field/id #uuid "27e31d3a-247b-506c-a5ca-66c30896d048" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ffef47e-2f1a-52ce-9ce8-8cc5126973d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437592} {:answer/id #uuid "82c17871-30b3-570d-9985-cbfb4030107c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82c17871-30b3-570d-9985-cbfb4030107c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437593} :answer-field/id #uuid "300b0a1c-8c14-56f6-b340-cad908fc709b" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2a6ca6d7-d1ef-5811-9457-4d7cf9a54890" :question/math-academy-id "q-119816" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x-2)^{2}(y+1)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(x-2)^{2}(y+1).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=2$ or $y=-1.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/ca/caa61190f1a5565c58838556529715c08f9f00402c6f4b3ccb99a914e748f198.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/d8/d836463631120853e05b3b5fb9e534822cf5611747a3eb17e22333901bfb8fd3.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative” is true. If $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $x>2$ and $y>-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative”; “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253625 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b3bfda0-2916-5df4-bd5f-f2782de4dd71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "168\\,\\mu \\text{g}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251577} {:answer/id #uuid "82a3dab9-6668-56a2-8f4a-1ac71ce2b87d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "185\\,\\mu \\text{g}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251655} {:answer/id #uuid "b28c00ea-9918-584e-b49c-c5b5a5a85322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "257\\,\\mu \\text{g}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252113} {:answer/id #uuid "f6cd46eb-92a2-58d1-b54c-803ce9781618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "178\\,\\mu \\text{g}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252709} {:answer/id #uuid "ff85d59b-ec71-5a51-ad43-ec8a736069bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "154\\,\\mu \\text{g}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6cd46eb-92a2-58d1-b54c-803ce9781618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "178\\,\\mu \\text{g}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252709} :answer-field/id #uuid "56ff4266-2fc4-5b74-8eff-cf31d811e76c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3c164d8d-6f7c-5364-9f24-9f1a44b57ac9" :question/math-academy-id "q-120002" :question/problem "Samarium-147 has a half-life of $106.1$ billion years. A sample of samarium-147 has an initial mass of $300\\,\\mu \\text{g}.$ Rounded to the nearest integer, what is the mass of the sample after $80$ billion years?" :question/worked-solution "The mass $M(t)$ of a radioactive substance at time $t$ can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)=-kM(t),\\,M(0)={M}_{0}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nM(t)={M}_{0}{e}^{-kt}.\n$$\n\nThe half-life ${t}_{1/2}$ is the time taken for the mass of the substance to reduce by one half and is given by\n\n$$\n{t}_{1/2}=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{k}.\n$$\n\nSince we know that ${t}_{1/2}=106.1$ billion years, we have\n\n$$\n106.1=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{k}\\,⇒\\,k=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{106.1}.\n$$\n\nAlso, since ${M}_{0}=300\\,\\mu \\text{g},$ we have the particular solution\n\n$$\nM(t)=300{e}^{-t\\operatorname{ln}⁡2/106.1}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nM(80)=300{e}^{-80\\operatorname{ln}⁡2/106.1}≈178\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that there will be $178\\,\\mu \\text{g}$ of the sample left."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253626 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b8416d-53d5-5e54-bf6f-c8aa2293c239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "300\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250698} {:answer/id #uuid "309619bf-ee0e-57f4-adfc-e5f1f208963f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250965} {:answer/id #uuid "8dc39acd-e2fd-50c2-bda5-993ba35b1fd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251754} {:answer/id #uuid "9a65b6c3-3bb9-5be9-b26b-b064dcaf24d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251878} {:answer/id #uuid "d012d83e-9640-56ad-a1bc-4c1efb098047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "309619bf-ee0e-57f4-adfc-e5f1f208963f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250965} :answer-field/id #uuid "437b0178-d996-500a-9085-a88d7cf6a389" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e6c4bf32-422c-5447-b557-5dce8db4fbab" :question/math-academy-id "q-120006" :question/problem "The half-life of astatine-223 is $50\\,\\text{s}.$ How long does it take for an $400\\,\\mu \\text{g}$ sample of astatine-223 to reduce to $50\\,\\mu \\text{g}?$" :question/worked-solution "The mass $M(t)$ of a radioactive substance at time $t$ can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)=-kM(t),\\,M(0)={M}_{0}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nM(t)={M}_{0}{e}^{-kt}.\n$$\n\nThe half-life ${t}_{1/2}$ is the time taken for the mass of the substance to reduce by one half and is given by\n\n$$\n{t}_{1/2}=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{k}.\n$$\n\nThere are two methods that we can use to solve this problem. We describe each of them below.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nSince we know that ${t}_{1/2}=50\\,\\text{s},$ we have\n\n$$\n50=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{k}\\,⇒\\,k=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{50}\n$$\n\nAlso, since ${M}_{0}=400\\,\\mu \\text{g},$ we have the particular solution\n\n$$\nM(t)=400{e}^{-t\\operatorname{ln}⁡2/50}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to calculate the time $t$ such that $M(t)=50\\,\\mu \\text{g}.$ So, we set up our equation as follows:\n\n$$\n50=400{e}^{-t\\operatorname{ln}⁡2/50}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}50 & =400{e}^{-t\\operatorname{ln}⁡2/50} \\\\ \\frac{50}{400} & ={e}^{-t\\operatorname{ln}⁡2/50} \\\\ \\frac{1}{8} & ={e}^{-t\\operatorname{ln}⁡2/50} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-t\\operatorname{ln}⁡2/50}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡8 & =-\\frac{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{50} \\\\ -\\operatorname{ln}⁡8 & =-\\frac{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{50} \\\\ t & =\\frac{50\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ t & =150.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that it takes $150\\,\\text{s}$ for the mass of the substance to reduce to $50\\,\\mu \\text{g}.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe wish to calculate the time $t$ such that $M(t)=50\\,\\mu \\text{g}.$ Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{M(t)}{M(0)} & =\\frac{50\\,\\mu \\text{g}}{400\\,\\mu \\text{g}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & ={\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\nM(t)={\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{3}\\cdot M(0).\n$$\n\nFrom this equation, we see that $3$ half-lives must have occurred for the mass to reduce from $400\\,\\mu \\text{g}$ to $50\\,\\mu \\text{g}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\nt=3\\cdot {t}_{1/2}=3\\cdot 50\\,\\text{s}=150\\,\\text{s}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that it takes $150\\,\\text{s}$ for the mass of the substance to reduce to $50\\,\\mu \\text{g}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262796 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78dc759e-2781-5f7c-8fdf-32c8a7488616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260936} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e65376-d802-5c70-a9b5-c7a733c9a942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261331} {:answer/id #uuid "bb19c345-96c8-5417-8091-0779682fa6e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261521} {:answer/id #uuid "e51f0554-9934-5f77-b1d4-2f9e022ea1c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261892} {:answer/id #uuid "e740a674-cf61-5f78-af1b-0865ebe203d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "62" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78dc759e-2781-5f7c-8fdf-32c8a7488616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260936} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7443e3d-bb79-5f31-9bc0-f76639543945" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1ea8f2b8-d1da-5f6e-96c2-1f49a78fce12" :question/math-academy-id "q-127578" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}5 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{vmatrix}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{vmatrix} & =5\\cdot 7-(-9)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =35-27 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262797 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2350f7db-d0b1-580d-8303-5d5534a14ce2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260185} {:answer/id #uuid "2f380174-748c-5220-b6ab-bb1fd86d6300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260300} {:answer/id #uuid "2fa4f15b-ff78-536d-9c98-39423cde1291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260305} {:answer/id #uuid "2fc2802a-b9f4-555c-a30c-fdb056782082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260307} {:answer/id #uuid "62c209ca-c14b-5357-9099-3070ded3b153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f380174-748c-5220-b6ab-bb1fd86d6300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260300} :answer-field/id #uuid "83ca020d-e4a7-5b74-b14e-0f4db14e8f9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bcfbc0ab-8a2a-5b55-a599-576a8e82d92e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127580" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & =-1\\cdot 5-(-10)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-5-20 \\\\  & =-25\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262800 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1729317d-f622-5dce-8c02-3f5018dcb8b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260077} {:answer/id #uuid "86f360a8-158d-58e7-8648-0876bd49a4c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3xy}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261052} {:answer/id #uuid "8a58d3cf-de39-5f9f-b770-d6d11f0da4b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261081} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d927b0-5361-5416-bb9f-d86d1935176e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5xy}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261316} {:answer/id #uuid "ac2d9a29-e850-51a7-ad56-c6faf0894dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a58d3cf-de39-5f9f-b770-d6d11f0da4b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261081} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c41b5de-ab83-554f-95bf-42d11f54be45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "26e4f5d9-b2df-5b89-afc1-259e97c4e9b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-127601" :question/problem "Calculate $det(C)$, if\n$$\n\\displaystyle C=\\begin{bmatrix}-x & -2y \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & 5y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-x & -2y \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & 5y\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-x\\cdot 5y-(-2y)\\cdot \\frac{x}{2} \\\\  & =-5xy+xy \\\\  & =-4xy\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262802 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5498ee4c-4372-5204-b6e1-f57f31f7ce72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{y}^{2}x-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260592} {:answer/id #uuid "61a3d195-a5ae-5921-ac90-3b4c24a6e5e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(2{x}^{2}+5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260716} {:answer/id #uuid "9ad83484-0f5d-5184-b122-b899402359be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}y+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261219} {:answer/id #uuid "9f32a52b-bd39-5040-afc5-c0f0787ecc96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261256} {:answer/id #uuid "a2a8698b-73f4-57ac-a21f-031d3c8b223a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(2{x}^{2}-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61a3d195-a5ae-5921-ac90-3b4c24a6e5e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(2{x}^{2}+5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260716} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1e2c382-0ce2-5adc-b135-69fb578a8e4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5adfe9df-8aee-5967-99f3-985aed9cc4da" :question/math-academy-id "q-127603" :question/problem "Calculate $det(D)$, if\n$$\n\\displaystyle D=\\begin{bmatrix}2x & y \\\\ -5 & xy\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2x & y \\\\ -5 & xy\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot xy-y\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y+5y \\\\  & =y(2{x}^{2}+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262803 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "231d65c4-afe9-5dda-9ec8-8e657ebc2e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260183} {:answer/id #uuid "2cde1f0f-ce43-5b48-8b5f-a4207965af8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260279} {:answer/id #uuid "2e9b7936-2a9f-5fa6-98b8-c2d31209e615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260296} {:answer/id #uuid "6e18de3f-d88f-51e5-8a5a-4c7a07f3003b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260842} {:answer/id #uuid "72f9541a-9495-523a-a73a-4a7b746e235a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cde1f0f-ce43-5b48-8b5f-a4207965af8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260279} :answer-field/id #uuid "469de0af-655e-5c52-99af-6a01835c14fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "eb9b1b8a-cede-5e44-9f81-ee8a71692716" :question/math-academy-id "q-127604" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 2k & -k+2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(U)=-1$, what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(U) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 2k & -k+2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-k+2)-(-5)\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =7k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-1$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-1 \\\\ 7k+6 & =-1 \\\\ 7k & =-1-6 \\\\ 7k & =-7 \\\\ k & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "613ae31f-3ed4-522f-b38e-30b725565300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260710} {:answer/id #uuid "6c66b584-1346-57a8-91c6-b84e73a70782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260826} {:answer/id #uuid "8ccc1966-d22e-5ca2-85e6-62f888a4ebc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v=\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261106} {:answer/id #uuid "dfbbb63f-c7de-5798-b663-aa393eb8f406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261850} {:answer/id #uuid "f645c953-47f3-5b1c-9345-c05fb1f18f37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v=\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c66b584-1346-57a8-91c6-b84e73a70782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260826} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ae8e73c-6de7-5bcc-a8b5-a2c66229f23e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7bb355a7-6406-51ad-b4a4-0aaf09eca17d" :question/math-academy-id "q-127606" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle T=\\begin{bmatrix}v & 2v \\\\ 2 & v+8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(T)=-4$, what is the value of $v?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =\\begin{vmatrix}v & 2v \\\\ 2 & v+8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =v\\cdot (v+8)-2v\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={v}^{2}+4v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(T)=-4$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =-4 \\\\ {v}^{2}+4v & =-4 \\\\ {v}^{2}+4v+4 & =0 \\\\ (v+2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ v & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aab353e-d8a2-5cee-ad8e-75d89f36942f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259969} {:answer/id #uuid "55f69ea5-658f-54da-aab9-eba230208482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260610} {:answer/id #uuid "77bbba7e-5eef-5fde-bf0b-27cf27e274ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260919} {:answer/id #uuid "e35430a5-8bd9-5cd3-a709-f9d32c9a6cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261873} {:answer/id #uuid "f83c7a76-e478-5e97-87ce-06f9facc6cc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77bbba7e-5eef-5fde-bf0b-27cf27e274ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260919} :answer-field/id #uuid "481e7819-63cc-5385-bd4b-6641777b91a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "612dd17c-57fb-5f36-b33a-8e40d39733fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-127607" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle P=\\begin{bmatrix}r-3 & r \\\\ 3 & r\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(P)=-9$, what is the value of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =\\begin{vmatrix}r-3 & r \\\\ 3 & r\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(r-3)\\cdot r-r\\cdot 3 \\\\  & ={r}^{2}-6r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(P)=-9$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =-9 \\\\ {r}^{2}-6r & =-9 \\\\ {r}^{2}-6r+9 & =0 \\\\ (r-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ r & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262806 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d8c86ed-6d17-58e5-80b8-58959792fbea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260000} {:answer/id #uuid "5da2ff79-d5ff-5f94-843d-fd01485931c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260680} {:answer/id #uuid "63782cc1-1e3c-5b15-9b88-3f08b7011